I've recorded a simple In-Game Movie of my upcoming hovercraft game. It ist still really early development, so dont expect shiny graphics .. :-p<br><br>It's in German at the moment, so I write a little of that what is showing up in the vid:<br><br>You see the hovercraft fully simluated by engine-thrust and real air-drag (with respect of vehicle angle!) - controlling is very precise and is one goal of the game. because it is fully simulated it is quite tricky to get the right feeling of steering, but in th end it is a lot of fun and challenging to get fast around where you should.<br><br>The whole game will be Multiplayer with big maps and many players (i have invested very much time in tweaking the network part) but i have to see how it performs in the end .. maybe i have to drop some of the simulations .. that's coming up - i hope to manage a minimum of 20 players per race.<br><br>Hope you like the little vid <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_wink.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=";-)" title="Wink"><br><br><a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QgEIYJea2A4" class="postlink">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QgEIYJea2A4</a><br><br>And thanks to the bullet guys - seems quite good<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8022">autofreax</a> — Sat Apr 16, 2011 3:24 pm</p><hr />
